From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:28:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibDevTools+LibWebCommon+LibWebView: Let the embedder name
 its directory

Profiles, crash reports, and the DevTools Firefox profile go in a
directory named "Ladybird" under the platform's config, data, cache, and
runtime directories. Another browser built on LibWebView shares them
with Ladybird when both are installed: their settings, history, and
cookies mix, each recovers the other's crash reports, and launching one
while the other runs on the same profile opens its URLs in the other.

WebView::set_application_name() names that directory instead. The
embedder calls it before anything reads it, which is before it creates
its Application, since the browser's crash handler is set up first.
Profiles given with --profile-path are where they were.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
